THIRD-PARTY DATA, MODELS AND GENE LISTS

None of the items below is shipped in this repository or in the package, except
where a derived table or a gene list is named. Each is obtained by the user from its
source, under its own terms.

* KRONOS2 (MahmoodLab, https://huggingface.co/MahmoodLab/KRONOS2), the image model of
  the optional [image] extra. CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, gated, non-commercial academic research
  only; commercial use of the model and its derivatives, including models trained on
  its outputs, needs prior approval from its authors. discell.image downloads the
  weights and the model's own code at run time with the user's own Hugging Face login
  (revision e2a5473206c02d9973885b6445ef783f7e082951 by default) and never
  redistributes them. Its non-commercial terms bind anyone who uses the image extra.
* BioLinkBERT-large (michiyasunaga/BioLinkBERT-large), downloaded by KRONOS2's own code
  on first use to encode the description of the 18S channel. Apache-2.0.
* KRONOS v1 (MahmoodLab), the image model behind the paper's fits. Deprecated by its
  authors and closed to new access requests; not supported or used by this release.
* 10x Genomics Xenium Prime datasets: FFPE Human Ovarian Cancer, FFPE Human Lung
  Cancer, Fresh Frozen Human Ovary. CC BY 4.0, attribution to 10x Genomics.
  reproduce/download.sh fetches them from 10x. The lineage maps in reproduce/labels/
  are derived from 10x's own labels and clusterings of these datasets.
* GEO series GSE315411 (the TMA core, slide 11, and its serial section, slide 10).
  Under the terms of its submitters on GEO. The in-house cell labels of the TMA core
  are not public and not shipped.
* The esophageal adenocarcinoma cohort of Yates et al. 2025 (Zenodo record 15341263),
  CC BY 4.0. Not downloaded or read by this package; reproduce/README.md documents how
  the paper used it, including program gene sets recovered from its published scores.
* CellChatDB (CellChatDB.human.rda, from CellChat, GPL-3). Downloaded by
  reproduce/download.sh and read as data by reproduce/scripts/lr_genes.py (with rdata,
  MIT); no CellChat code is imported or copied, and neither the database nor the
  derived ligand-receptor gene list is shipped.
* The S and G2/M cell-cycle genes of Tirosh et al. 2016, as updated in Seurat's
  cc.genes.updated.2019 (Seurat: MIT). The gene symbols are listed in
  src/discell/sensitivity/findings.py; the scoring reimplements Scanpy's score_genes
  (BSD-3-Clause), with no Scanpy code imported.

DEPENDENCIES

The core dependencies (numpy, scipy, pandas, torch, scikit-learn, threadpoolctl,
anndata, h5py, pyarrow, shapely) are under permissive licenses (BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0,
PSF), with two small MPL-2.0 packages pulled in by anndata. The [image] extra adds
tifffile, zarr, huggingface-hub, transformers and omegaconf (BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0);
its restrictions come with the KRONOS2 weights and code, not with these packages. No
GPL code is imported or vendored.
